      "textEn": "434\n\nWith the songs of the dance, the conches, the drums, and the flutes. 7. Meaning of the word:\n\nToyaih - with water necessary for washing the lotus feet and bathing; Samarhanaih - for the worship of God, the foot washing, Arghya etc.\nFrom materials; with garlands of flowers; with sandalwood and agarwood, to apply on the body of Lord Vamanadeva; by applying paste; by incense; by lamps; with fragrant flowers; with sprouts; by akshat (unbroken rice grains);\nBy akshat; by fruits; by roots and sprouts; by hymns; by cheers; with victory cries; with\nThat-virya-mahima-angikitaih (images) that indicate the glorious deeds of God; by dance, musical instruments, and songs; with dance, From the musical instruments,\nFrom the playing and singing of songs; Shankha—conch; Dundubhi—Dundubhi; Nishwanaih—from sound..\n\nThey worshiped God with fragrant flowers, water, footwear, and offerings, sandalwood paste, and agarwood paste, incense, lamp, lava,\nAkshat, fruit, root, and sprout.\nWhile doing so, they praised and celebrated the successful works of God. In this way, while worshiping God,\nthey danced, played instruments, sang, and blew conches and drums. Jambavanrajastu bherishabdai rmanojavah. Victory to the righteous, the festival is proclaimed in all. Meaning of the word:\n\nJambavan—Jambavan; Riksha-rajah tu—King of the Rikshas; Bheri-shabdaah—By playing the Bheri; Manah-javaah—In a state of mind; Vijayam—Victory, triumph; Dikshu—In all directions; Sarvasu—Everywhere; Maha-utsavam—A grand festival; Aghoshayat—Proclaimed. King of the bears, Jambavan also joined the celebrations. He announced the victory of Lord Vamanadeva by sounding the bugle in all directions. Having seen all the gods, I have become blind.\nO! He who is initiated by the gods, who is endowed with the gods. 9. Meaning of the word:\n\nMahim—to the earth; Sarvam—all; Hritam—chiseled; Dristva—by seeing; Tri-Pad-Vyaj-Yachnaya—only three steps to ask for land;\nUchu—said; Swa-Bhartuh—owner;